# ls-foundry boundary (EXIFilixir)

**Never** create, edit, commit, or publish files under `~/projects/ls-foundry` (or any clone of [ls-foundry](https://github.com/jeffgo10/ls-foundry)) from an **exifilixir** agent session. Engine changes belong to an **ls-foundry agent** only.

This repo may consume published `@jeffgo10/*` packages (GitHub Packages). Prefer `/update-ls-foundry-packages` after a release. Do not vendor or copy package source into this repo.

## Consumer packages (EXIFilixir)

Primary fit for 360° preview / shared utilities:

| Package | Role | Notes | Pin |
|---|---|---|---|
| `@jeffgo10/panorama-viewer` | React equirectangular viewer (Pannellum) | Client-only; import `styles.css`; `transpilePackages` in Next; `dynamic(..., { ssr: false })` | `0.1.2` |
| `@jeffgo10/helpers` | Shared helpers | Subpaths: `brand`, `browser`, `clipboard`, `gestures`, `image`, `text`, `ui` — prefer these over re-implementing | `1.5.0` |

Optional / unlikely here unless product expands:

| Package | When |
|---|---|
| `@jeffgo10/gl-viewer` | LiDAR / WebXR / Three.js demos (see LiteShade Media) |
| `@jeffgo10/react-canvas-designer`, `shared-types`, `canvas-upscaler` | StickPak canvas/print pipeline — not EXIFilixir |

**Pins:** when packages are added, record exact versions in `package.json` and update this table. Exact pins (no `^`) need an explicit version bump via `/update-ls-foundry-packages`.

## Auth for GitHub Packages

- Copy `.npmrc.example` → `.npmrc` and set `GITHUB_TOKEN` (classic PAT with `read:packages`).
- Never commit a `.npmrc` that embeds a raw token.
- Never commit the token into rules, PRs, or handoffs.

## When EXIFilixir needs engine work

1. Do **not** patch ls-foundry yourself.
2. Give the user a **paste-ready brief** for the ls-foundry agent (template below).
3. After publish, run `/update-ls-foundry-packages` here and wire the app.

## Paste template — ls-foundry agent

```text
## Task — <short title>

Repo: jeffgo10/ls-foundry.

### Goal
<what EXIFilixir needs and why — e.g. panorama preview API, helpers/image util>

### Required work
1. Packages / versions to bump (likely panorama-viewer and/or helpers)
2. API / type / CSS export changes
3. Publish to GitHub Packages; confirm npm view dependencies

### Out of scope
- exifilixir UI / Firebase Functions

### Done when
- Published versions + deps verified
- Tell consumer: run /update-ls-foundry-packages in exifilixir
```

## Do not

- Edit, commit, or `pnpm publish` from ls-foundry while working in exifilixir
- Duplicate panorama-viewer / helpers logic in-repo “just for now”
- Assume `npm update` jumps exact pins — bump versions explicitly when needed
